yc8|n|Honor; honorableness; dignity; propriety; suitableness; decency. ; The quality or state of being honest; probity; fairness and straightforwardness of conduct, speech, etc.; integrity; sincerity; truthfulness; freedom from fraud or guile. ; Chastity; modesty. ; Satin flower; the name of two cruciferous herbs having large flat pods, the round shining partitions of which are more beautiful than the blossom; -- called also lunary and moonwort. Lunaria biennis is common honesty; L. rediva is perennial honesty.	a:tml,10,3~tml,10,3	N:x2k,59,3;1jyl,42,7~1jyl,42,7;x2k,59,3
